  "startingSkills": {
    "_note": "⚠️ SNG-339 §2. What a character KNOWS HOW TO DO before anyone teaches them a craft. Keyed on the action-tag vocabulary the game already uses — the same 54 tags authored on item.bonusTags — so a background's training and a trade's tools answer the same question in the same words. No ninth vocabulary.",
    "grantCap": 2,
    "usesPerRank": 25,
    "maxRank": 2,
    "_theRule": "A background grants what that LIFE taught, and a tradition grants what the CRAFT needs alongside itself. They stack to a cap of 2, so a hunter of the horizon is genuinely better at scouting than either alone — and no combination exceeds the cap, which is what stops a build reaching rank 3 at creation.",
    "_whyTwoEach": "Two tags per source, never more. ⚠️ A background is a LIFE, not a career package: an orphan learned to move unseen and to go without, and everything else they picked up later belongs to play.",
    "_orphanNote": "⚠️ ERIK'S CASE. `orphan` grants stealth + survival — which is what the shadow aptitude's -3 social was, until now, THE ONLY EXPRESSION OF. The penalty stays and stops being the whole story.",
